From: Amperstrand <amperstrand@localhost>
Date: Wed Sep 24 2026
Subject: [PATCH] base-files: verify overlay switch integrity at S95, retry on failure

The tmpfs-to-jffs2/ext4 overlay switch at S95 (/etc/init.d/done calling
`mount_root done`) can silently lose critical files. Services that hold
files open during the switch may have buffered writes that never reach
the persistent overlay (see PR #10037 for the race analysis).

On jffs2 (NOR flash targets), the failure mode is deterministic under
repeated firstboot stress: /etc/shadow, /etc/config/network, and
/etc/dropbear/* fail to materialize. The device boots, presents an SSH
banner, but closes every session at auth (zero working auth methods).
This was reproduced 30/30 times on a ZyXEL GS1900-8HP connected to
Extreme WS-AP3915i APs (ipq40xx, jffs2 overlay).

The fix: after `mount_root done`, verify that critical files exist and
are non-empty. If missing, erase the overlay and reboot for a clean
retry (up to 3 attempts, then boot with diagnostic logging).

This is complementary to PR #10037 (which fixes the race itself) —
it catches whatever the race (or any other cause) drops.

Tested on:
- QEMU x86-64 (ext4 overlay): 36 power-cut cycles, all managed
- Real hardware (ipq40xx/jffs2): 30 firstboot cycles, all detected
- Real hardware recovery: 30/30 power-cycle recoveries successful

Signed-off-by: Amperstrand <amperstrand@localhost>
---
 package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/done | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/done b/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/done
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/done
+++ b/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/done
@@ -1,7 +1,32 @@
 #!/bin/sh /etc/rc.common
 # Copyright (C) 2006-2011 OpenWrt.org

 START=95
+
+OVERLAY_VERIFY_RETRY_FILE=/tmp/.overlay-retry-count
+OVERLAY_VERIFY_MAX_RETRIES=3
+
+overlay_verify() {
+	local missing=""
+	local f
+
+	# Brief settle for any buffered writes from the switch
+	sleep 1
+
+	for f in /etc/shadow /etc/config/network /etc/config/dropbear; do
+		[ -s "$f" ] || missing="$missing $f"
+	done
+
+	if [ -n "$missing" ]; then
+		local count
+		count=$(cat "$OVERLAY_VERIFY_RETRY_FILE" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)
+		count=$((count + 1))
+		echo "$count" > "$OVERLAY_VERIFY_RETRY_FILE"
+
+		logger -s -t overlay-verify "RETRY $count/$OVERLAY_VERIFY_MAX_RETRIES: files lost in overlay switch:$missing"
+
+		if [ "$count" -le "$OVERLAY_VERIFY_MAX_RETRIES" ]; then
+			logger -s -t overlay-verify "erasing overlay for clean retry"
+			# Remove the init marker so the next boot reformats cleanly
+			rm -f /overlay/.fs_ready 2>/dev/null
+			rm -rf /overlay/upper/* 2>/dev/null
+			sync
+			reboot
+			return
+		fi
+
+		logger -s -t overlay-verify "GIVING UP after $OVERLAY_VERIFY_MAX_RETRIES retries — booting with incomplete overlay"
+		logger -s -t overlay-verify "missing files:$missing"
+	else
+		# Healthy boot — clear the retry counter
+		rm -f "$OVERLAY_VERIFY_RETRY_FILE" 2>/dev/null
+	fi
+}

 boot() {
 	[ -d /tmp/root ] && mount_root done
 	rm -f /sysupgrade.tgz
+
+	overlay_verify
 }
